{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-30T23:41:34.002Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7b0e58428f53e3aaeaafb372","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-m6ig79","lineage:pm-m6ig79","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-m6ig79","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-m6ig79","lineage:pm-m6ig79","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.312","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Fix in src/cli/error-guidance.ts: renderBoundedGuidanceMessage renders progressively compacted candidates following the declared ladder (drop Why, limit collections, compact the recovery bundle to suggested_retry under 400 bytes plus missing/allowed values/next_best_command, then bound the What happened text to 320 code points) and appends an omission notice; only text that still overflows falls through to the SDK action-only projection. The public projectPmDiagnosticText contract is unchanged. src/sdk/lifecycle/create.ts now says --unset cannot satisfy a required scalar option and that only repeatable options accept an explicit --clear-* empty set."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-4oc353"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Text refusals drop the specific What happened detail when an echoed argv overflows the diagnostic ceiling"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The JSON diagnostic projection walks the declared ladder (full, omit_explanation, limit_collections, compact_recovery, action_only), but the human text path jumped straight from full to action_only. A refusal whose recovery bundle echoed a long attempted command (for example a 400-word --description) therefore printed only the generic title, the generic What is required line and an overflow notice, and dropped the one sentence that said what was wrong. Reproduced on 2026.10.30 with strict create plus --unset assignee: the short invocation names the problem, the long one does not. The same refusal also claimed --clear-* directives cannot satisfy required options, while repeatable options such as --clear-deps do satisfy them."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"in_progress"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","diagnostics","output-budget"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-30T23:41:34.002Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-30T23:41:34.002Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A text refusal whose full rendering exceeds the error text ceiling keeps the What happened detail and the missing flags whenever a ladder stage fits; it drops the attempted_command echo before the detail; it names the omission and points to --json; an oversized detail is bounded rather than removed; short refusals are byte-identical; the strict create refusal states the scalar/repeatable rule accurately; regression tests fail without the fix"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Agents reading text refusals see what was wrong even when their own long input overflows the diagnostic ceiling."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-cha95z","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:41:34.002Z","author":"ha